(footprint "SW_MX_HotSwap_THT_2.75u_MXPCBStab_Diode" (version 20221018) (generator pcbnew)
  (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "Cherry MX style mechanical keyboard switch, Kailh/Gateron hot-swap socket and through-hole soldering, single-sided mounting. Plate cut lines: User.1=15.60mm square (cosmetic cover, all switches), User.2=14.00mm square (MX / MX Low Profile / Gateron Low Profile). Keycap: 2.75u (courtyard 52.34x19.00mm). Cherry MX PCB-mount stabilizer holes included. Stabilizer plate cut on User.5 (fits plate-mount and PCB-mount MX stabilizers). Series diode pads on back side: pad 3 = anode, pad 4 = cathode (cathode bar on B.SilkS, body outline on B.Fab, cathode points up). Combined hand-soldering land for SOD-123 / SOD-323 / MiniMELF (LL-34, LL4148): 2.0x1.4mm pads at +/-1.6mm axial offset. With the bundled SW_Key_Diode symbol pins 2 and 3 are stacked (one net), so the switch-diode series circuit is complete at schematic level; on the PCB route the short pad 2 - pad 3 track shown by the ratsnest, and wire the matrix to pads 1 and 4.")
  (tags "switch, hot_swap, diode")
